External Protocol Setup for Citadel 68K

Setup for XPR Zmodem and Kermit:

 1) Put the XPRD program on your path.  This is the same one in the Fred
    Fish archive(69x, can't remember which one!).  I only included the
    executable, If you want the source and doc file, I have it on the
    Amiga Zone or get the Fish disk.
    I have a directory with all my extra commands, it is on my path and
    I put the program in there.
 2) Put the CTDLPROT.SYS file in the room area.  It must be there when
    Citadel starts up.
 3) copy the two XPR libraries into your libs: directory.  Be careful not
    to change the case of the names, the libraries are case sensitive!
 4) restart your Citadel, you will now have Zmodem and Kermit as external
    protocols!

 Other XPR libraries can be used.  The letters H, and Q are available
 for other protocol if you find another additional XPR libraries you
 wish to use.

 This should work with any Citadel 68k version.  If you
 have questions, feel free to contact me in the Citadel 68K or Amiga
 rooms or call the Amiga Zone at 609-953-8159.

